🔁 Pattern 1: Simple Traversal Pattern

Idea: Node-by-node move karo using temp pointer

🔹 Used In:

Print linked list

Count nodes

Search an element

Find length

Node temp = head;
while(temp != null){
    temp = temp.next;
}


⏱ Time: O(n)
📦 Space: O(1)

🔄 Pattern 2: Reversal Pattern (3-Pointer)

Idea: Direction of next pointer reverse karo

🔹 Used In:

Reverse linked list

Reverse sublist

Reverse in k-groups

Palindrome linked list

Node prev = null;
Node curr = head;

while(curr != null){
    Node next = curr.next;
    curr.next = prev;
    prev = curr;
    curr = next;
}
head = prev;


📌 Golden Pattern ⭐
⏱ Time: O(n) | Space: O(1)

🐢🐇 Pattern 3: Slow–Fast Pointer (Tortoise–Hare)

Idea: Ek pointer 1 step, dusra 2 steps

🔹 Used In:

Find middle of linked list

Detect cycle

Remove cycle

Check palindrome

Happy number (LL type logic)

slow = fast = head;
while(fast != null && fast.next != null){
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next.next;
}


⏱ Time: O(n)
📦 Space: O(1)

🔁 Pattern 4: Cycle Detection Pattern

Algorithm: Floyd’s Cycle Detection

🔹 Used In:

Detect loop

Find start of loop

Remove loop

while(fast != null && fast.next != null){
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next.next;
    if(slow == fast) return true;
}


📌 Interview Favourite

🔙 Pattern 5: Nth Node from End (Gap Pattern)

Idea: Two pointers ke beech n ka gap maintain karo

🔹 Used In:

Remove nth node from end

Find nth node from end

fast = slow = head;
for(int i=0;i<n;i++) fast = fast.next;

while(fast != null){
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next;
}


⏱ Time: O(n)

🔗 Pattern 6: Merge Two Linked Lists

Idea: Dummy node + comparison

🔹 Used In:

Merge two sorted lists

Merge k sorted lists

Sort linked list

Node dummy = new Node(-1);
Node curr = dummy;

while(l1 != null && l2 != null){
    if(l1.data < l2.data){
        curr.next = l1;
        l1 = l1.next;
    } else {
        curr.next = l2;
        l2 = l2.next;
    }
    curr = curr.next;
}


📌 Dummy Node = Cleaner code

